# Chat Response Formatting

When ending with a Context Checkpoint, keep it visually small and plain.

- Do not format the checkpoint title or labels as Markdown headings.
- Do not use bold text, blockquotes, tables, or code fences for the checkpoint.
- Use plain text labels: `Context Checkpoint`, `Task:`, `What I Did:`, and `What I Need From You:`.
- Keep the checkpoint concise enough to scan in 10 seconds.
